  "question": {
    "text": "When dil. sulphuric acid reacts with aqueous solution of potassium chromate, the colour changes from yellow to orange. This shows that"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "chromate ions reduced",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "chromate ions are oxidised",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "monocentric complex is converted into dicentric complex",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "oxygen gets removed from chromate ions",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>On acidification of potassium chromate solution, yellow colour changes to orange colour due to formation of dichromate which suggests that monocentric complex is converted into dicentric complex.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CrO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><munder><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow><mfenced><mtext>Dil.</mtext></mfenced></munder><mo>&#10230;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p>"
